# Q3: Structure Comparison. Compare 2+ full primitive sequences (e.g., M1: pose > movement > pose vs M2: pose > path > path). State the winner and why—**prioritize movement/path beats that express the cue**, not pose-only tweaks.
# Q3: M1: `pose` (hands together) > `movement` (torso/head bow) > `pose` (hold bow). This is a clear three-beat structure: set the pose, perform the action, hold for emphasis. M2: `pose` (arms apart) > `path` (bring hands together) > `movement` (bow). This is more complex and less direct. Winner: M1, because the core of the gesture is the bow from the prayer-like hand position, so establishing that pose cleanly first is the most effective approach.
# Q4: Context Reinforcement. Compare 2+ micro-timing choices (speed, repetition, hold_time, torso/head expression) that make the gesture read stronger and pick the best one.
